 "_about": "The owner hears a volume swell at the 2nd note of each slur in bar 2 of Whence 12-TET, Celli (Celli - Performance): four slurs of four 136 ms sixteenths, pitches 51 52 51 49. Measured 2026-10-12 on the Windows test VM: kthost (C:\\claude\\kt, MD5 ea7e692e) offline, Kontakt 8 + SSO, Celli - Performance from MuseScore's resaved setup (library defaults). Events: the fork's dumpEvents (tst_liveequivalence, integrate-1012 build, shipped map, Recommended) of Celli - Performance, bars 1-2 and bar 3's first note (seconds 0-4.40, bar 1 as lead-in so bar 2's first note is a transition as in the score), played twice (passes at 1.0 s and 9.0 s, round robins advancing); four variants (variants). Per note of bar 2 (16 notes = 4 slurs, per pass): rms* = mean-square level of the mono mix in dB full scale, perceived* = mean of the perceived-loudness envelope (tools/playbackverify/loudness.py perceived_envelope, 33.2 log10 scale, ~dB), each over 136.4 ms: *Written from the note-on, *Arrival from the note-on plus the map's Celli - Performance legatoDelay for the interval from the note before (arrivalMs; the sound of a transition arrives ~200-240 ms after its note-on, so the arrival window is the note as heard). means: per slur position (1-4) over 4 slurs x 2 passes. envelope10ms: pass 1's perceived envelope from bar 2's start, 10 ms steps. Result: in every variant the slur's 2nd and 3rd notes are ~2.2 dB louder than its 1st and ~3-4 dB louder than its 4th (perceived, arrival windows); removing the CC11 127s changes nothing (A vs C within 0.2 dB), fingered instead of bowed first transitions raises notes 1 and 4 by ~0.8-1.2 dB but leaves the 1st-to-2nd rise (2.1-2.3 dB). With B+C (D) Kontakt receives identical events but for pitch, so the swell is the samples' own level along 49 -> 51 -> 52 -> 51 -> 49 (51 reached from 49 quieter than 51 reached from 52; 49 the quietest), not MuseScore's CC11 or transition choice. Branch smooth-onset-timing (Task 2); the renderer does not read this file.",
